"Learn about the Audible Standard Membership (https://help.audible.com/s/article/learn-about-standard-plan?language=en_US)\nciteturn767search0 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2 weeks ago; Crawled: 2 days ago; Note: If you sign up with a 30-day free trial, your Audible Standard membership will automatically renew and you'll be charged the regular monthly price after 30 days. ...   * Download your selected audiobooks for offline listening.\n\n## Learn about the Audible Standard Membership\n\n  * Oct 6, 2026\n\nLearn about the Audible Standard Membership\n\nURL Name\n\nlearn-about-standard-plan\n\nAnswer\n\nAudible Standard is a monthly membership where you can select one new audiobook each month from the entire Audible collection of 1 million titles without using credits.\n\nWith an Audible Standard monthly subscription, you can:\n\n  * Select a credit-free monthly audiobook: You can select 1 audiobook a month from the entire Audible collection of 1 million titles and grow your Library over time, and it's yours to keep in your Library as long as your membership is active.\n  * Access podcasts: Unlimited listening to podcasts and early access to new episodes of select shows. The access to podcasts is complimentary in addition to your monthly selection.\n  * Listen anywhere: You can download titles in your Library through the Audible app (downloads aren't available on the website) and listen to them without being connected to the internet.\n  * Pause your membership: You can pause your membership for 30, 60, or 90 days (up to 90 days total every 12 months). During your pause, you won't receive new monthly listens and your previously selected monthly listens will be temporarily locked in your Library. You can still listen to purchased titles and buy new audiobooks. Learn more about pausing your membership. \n  * Access great deals: Enjoy our Daily Deals and special sales (though some member-exclusive sales are reserved for Premium).\n  * Purchase titles: You can buy any audiobook using your credit/debit card and keep it forever, even after cancellation. Any unused credit from your previous Premium membership or gift credits can still be used for purchases.\n\nNotes:\n\n  * You can pause your Audible Standard membership or cancel at any time.\n  * The ability to select a monthly audiobook doesn't roll over to the next month. This means if you miss a month, you'll still only have 1 monthly audiobook selection the next month. Be sure to make a new selection each month to get the full value of your membership.\n  * Memberships billed through the Google Play Store can be paused for 30, 60, or 90 days; memberships billed through the Apple App Store can only be paused for 30 days. For information on how to pause your membership through these platforms, please refer to Manage App Store subscription and Manage Google Play Store subscription.\n\n## How do I sign up for Audible Standard membership?\n\nYou can sign up for the Audible Standard membership in the Audible app and on the Audible site.\n\nOn the Audible website\n\n  1. Go to the Audible site.\n  2. Select Get started.\n  3. Select Sign up for Standard.\n  4. You may be asked to sign in with your Amazon account.\n  5. Select Start now.\n\nNote: If you sign up with a 30-day free trial, your Audible Standard membership will automatically renew and you'll be charged the regular monthly price after 30 days. You can cancel anytime from your Membership details page.\n\nIn the app\n\n  1. Go to your Profile.\n  2. Select the Settings gear icon.\n  3. Under Membership, select Details.\n  4. Select Sign up for Standard.\n  5. Select Start now.\n\nNote: You can cancel anytime from your app settings. For more details, please see  Manage App Store subscription and Manage Google Play Store subscription.\n\n## How do I sign up for an Audible Standard trial?\n\nYou can sign up for a 30-day free trial if you haven't been an Audible member or taken a free trial in the last 12 months.\n\nOn the Audible website\n\n  11. Go to the Audible site.\n  12. Select Try Standard free.\n  13. You may be asked to sign in with your Amazon account.\n  14. Select Try Standard free to confirm your subscription.\n\nIn the app\n\n  15. Open the Audible app.\n  16. Sign in with your Amazon account.\n  17. Select Try Standard free.\n  18. Select Try for $0.00 to confirm your subscription.\n\nAfter 30 days, your membership will automatically renew and you'll be charged the regular monthly price. You can cancel anytime from your Membership details page.\n\nNote:\n\n  * While you won't be charged for your free trial, the trial membership is converted to a paid membership plan at the end of the trial period. You can change your membership status at any time through your Membership details page.\n  * If your membership is billed through Google Play or Apple you will need to cancel from your App Store or Google Play Store.\n\n## What is a monthly audiobook selection or monthly title?\n\nMonthly audiobook selections are any title you select as part of your Audible Standard membership benefit. With Audible Standard membership, you can select 1 audiobook a month and grow your Library collection over time.\n\nMonthly audiobook selections are available in your Library until you cancel. Once you cancel, you will no longer have access to titles you selected with this membership.\n\nIf you miss a monthly selection, your ability to select 1 monthly audiobook doesn't roll over to the next month.\n\nNote: Audible Standard membership includes access to our podcast collection. These ad-free podcasts are available in addition to your monthly audiobook selection, and you'll have early access to new episodes of select shows as they're released.\n\n## How do I cancel my Audible Standard membership?\n\nWhen you cancel your membership, you'll lose access to all titles that you received through your monthly selections at the end of your final billing cycle. You'll still have access to titles purchased with Audible credits or cash.\n\nAfter your plan is cancelled, any monthly audiobook selections in your Library will have a 🔒 lock icon next to them and you will see a message that a title is no longer available if you try to play it.\n\nHowever, you can still purchase that title if you'd like to own it or become a member again to regain access. If no purchase options are available, we no longer carry the title.\n\nAs an Audible Standard member you can switch to other Audible plans anytime from the Audible site or through the Google Play Store or App Store. For more details, please visit Switch plans.\n\nNote: If you signed up on the Audible website, please see Cancel membership to learn more. If you signed up in the Audible app, visit Manage App Store subscription or Manage Google Play Store subscription for more details.\n\n## Can I return or exchange my monthly audiobook selections?\n\nMonthly audiobook selections aren't eligible for return or exchange. If you're having an issue playing or listening to your monthly selection, you can try these playback troubleshooting steps.\n\n## What if I don't select a monthly audiobook one month?\n\nIf you miss a month, your ability to select 1 monthly audiobook doesn't roll over to the next month. You can always see the date by which you need to make your monthly audiobook selection on your Membership details page on the Audible site or in your Profile in the app.\n\n## Can I listen to Audible titles with the Amazon Prime subscription?\n\nAudible is not included with an Amazon Prime subscription. You will need to purchase a separate Audible membership. However, Prime members do get some Audible benefits. You can try Audible Premium free and get two free audiobooks.\n\n## What membership plans does Audible offer?\n\nAudible offers monthly and annual membership plans.\n\nMonthly memberships\n\nPlan  | Benefits\nAudible Standard  | \n\n  * Select 1 audiobook a month from our entire collection.\n  * Download your selected audiobooks for offline listening.\n  * Get unlimited access to podcasts.\n  * Listen to your selected audiobooks until you cancel. Unused monthly selections don't roll over to the next month.\nAudible Premium – 1 Credit  | \n\n  * 1 credit per month to be used to redeem any title from our entire collection of titles.\n  * Titles you buy with a credit are yours to keep even if you cancel your membership.\n  * Access to unlimited streaming and listening from the included catalog.\n  * Exclusive sales and discounts on purchased titles.\nAudible Premium – 2 Credits  | \n\n  * 2 credits per month to be used to redeem any title from our entire collection of titles.\n  * Titles you buy with a credit are yours to keep even if you cancel your membership.\n  * Access to unlimited streaming and listening from the included catalog.\n  * Exclusive sales and discounts on purchased titles.\n\nAnnual memberships\n\nPlan  | Benefits\nAudible Premium Annual – 12 Credits  | \n\n  * 12 credits at time of purchase to be used to redeem any title from our entire collection of titles.\n  * Titles you buy with a credit are yours to keep even if you cancel your membership.\n  * Access to unlimited streaming and listening from the included catalog.\n  * Exclusive sales and discounts on purchased titles.\nAudible Premium Annual – 24 Credits  | \n\n  * 24 credits at time of purchase to be used to redeem any title from our entire collection of titles.\n  * Titles you buy with a credit are yours to keep even if you cancel your membership.\n  * Access to unlimited streaming and listening from the included catalog.\n  * Exclusive sales and discounts on purchased titles.\n\nNotes:\n\n  * If your subscription is billed through the Google Play Store or App Store, the price may differ from what's shown in Audible.com. Payments are handled directly by Google or Apple. You can manage your Audible subscription in their respective app stores.\n  * Visit the Audible membership benefits page to view all Audible membership plans, prices, and benefits details.\n  * Membership prices may vary due to special offers and deals.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nLearn about the Audible Premium Membership (https://help.audible.com/s/article/learn-about-premium-plus?language=en_GB)\nciteturn767search1 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2 months ago; Crawled: last month; You can also download your titles to listen offline. ... Visit our help center article to learn more about Audible credits. ... Note: If you sign up with a 30-day free trial, your membership will automatically renew and you’ll be charged the regular monthly price after 30 days.\n\n## Learn about the Audible Premium Membership\n\n  * Aug 20, 2026\n  * Knowledge\n\nTitle\n\nLearn about the Audible Premium Membership\n\nURL Name\n\nlearn-about-premium-plus\n\nAnswer\n\n \n\nThe name of our Premium Plus plan is changing to Premium. You may see both names used while our site is updated. Don’t worry, nothing else has changed and your member benefits remain the same.\n\n \n\nAudible is a spoken word audio entertainment company owned by Amazon. You can find many types of titles with different voices. You can easily search, save, and buy audiobooks you like. You can listen to your audiobooks through the Audible app, online player, or any compatible MP3 player.\n\nIf you like to listen to bestsellers and new releases, you might like this plan. With a regular Premium Plus monthly membership, you have access to:\n\n  * Credits: You'll receive monthly credits to buy any audiobook you want, even new releases. Running low on credits? You can buy extra credits when you run out.\n  * Finding and playing titles: It's easy to browse through audiobooks, podcasts, and Originals in the Audible library. You can stream all you want from the Plus Catalog. Want to buy individual titles? You can do that too, whether you're a member or not.\n  * Ways to listen: You can enjoy Audible content through the mobile app or online player. You can also download your titles to listen offline.\n  * Cancellation and pausing: You can cancel your plan anytime, and you can pause your Premium membership if needed. Remember that if you cancel, you'll lose access to Plus Catalog titles and any unused credits.\n  * Members-only sales and deals: you will get access to exclusive sales and deals.\n\nNote: Premium monthly membership has two options: 1 credit a month or 2 credits a month. Premium annual memberships are also available in 12 or 24 credit plans. With annual membership, you get access to all of your credits right away. Any title you get with a credit is yours to keep. Visit our Audible membership benefits page to view prices and benefit details. Visit our help center article to learn more about Audible credits.\n\n## How do I sign up for Premium membership?\n\nYou can sign up for Premium membership from the Audible site or through the app.\n\n### On desktop\n\n  1. Go to the Audible site.\n  2. Select Browse.\n  3. Select Plans & pricing.\n  4. Select the Audible Premium plan. You may be asked to sign in with your Amazon account.\n  5. Confirm your subscription.\n\nNote: If you sign up with a 30-day free trial, your membership will automatically renew and you’ll be charged the regular monthly price after 30 days. You can cancel anytime from your Account details page.  \n\n### In the app \n\n  1. Go to your Profile.\n  2. Select the Settings gear icon.\n  3. In the Membership section, select Details.\n  4. Select Start now. \nNote: You will be taken out of the app momentarily and redirected to Audible.com to complete the enrollment. \n  5. Select Start now. \n\nNote: You can cancel anytime. If your membership is billed through Google Play or the Apple you will need to c ancel from your  App Store or Google Play Store settings at least 24 hours in advance.   \n\n## How do I sign up for Premium trial?\n\nNew customers can sign up for a Premium free trial from the Audible site or through the app for iOS users. After 30 days, your membership will automatically renew and you’ll be charged the regular monthly price. You can cancel anytime from your Account details page.\n\n### On desktop\n\n  1. Go to the Audible site.\n  2. Select the Premiumplan.\n  3. Select Start my free trial.\n  4. Sign in with your Amazon account.\n  5. Select your payment method.\n  6. Select Try for $0.00.   \n\n### In the app:\n\n  1. Open the Audible app.\n  2. Sign in with your Amazon account.\n  3. Select Join. \n  4. Select Try for $0.00.\nNote: You will be taken out of the app momentarily and redirected to Audible.com to complete the enrollment. \n  5. Select Start now.\n\nNote: You can cancel anytime from your Account details page. If your membership is billed through Google Play or the Apple you will need to c ancel from your App Store or Google Play. Remember, if you cancel your Audible membership you’ll lose access to member benefits like exclusive discounts, included titles in the Plus Catalog, and credits.\n\n## What is the Premium plan member discount benefit?\n\nAs a Premium member, you get an exclusive discount every time you buy an audiobook beyond your monthly credit. With this member discount benefit, you‘ll always pay less than the non-member price on every title in our catalog.\n\n### What are the different ways I can purchase audiobooks?\n\nAs a Premium member, you have several options:\n\n  * Use your monthly or annual credits - can be used on any audiobook, regardless of price. Credits are deposited into your account at the start of each billing cycle.\n  * Pay the member-discounted price — if you've already used your credit for the month, you can purchase any audiobook at your exclusive member price.\n  * Buy extra credits — if you're eligible, you can purchase a single credit or a bundle of credits for extra savings.\n\nYou'll see all available options on title detail pages and at checkout.\n\n### How does the member discount work?\n\nYour member discount is applied automatically to every audiobook in our collection. The discount varies by title, so you'll save more on some audiobooks and less on others—but you'll always pay less than the non-member price.\n\n## What membership plans does Audible offer?\n\nAudible offers monthly and annual membership plans.\n \n\nMonthly Membership  | Membership Benefits\nAudible Plus  | \n\n  * $7.95/month\n  * Access to unlimited streaming and listening from the Audible Plus Catalog\n  * Available only for current Audible Plus members\nAudible Premium – 1 Credit  | \n\n  * $14.95/month\n  * 1 credit per month to be used to redeem any title from our Premium selections\n  * Access to unlimited streaming and listening from the Audible Plus Catalog\n  * Exclusive sales and discounts on purchased titles\nAudible Premium – 2 Credits  | \n\n  * $22.95/month\n  * 2 credits per month to be used to redeem any title from our Premium selections\n  * Access to unlimited streaming and listening from the Audible Plus Catalog\n  * Exclusive sales and discounts on purchased titles\nAudible Standard  | \n\n  * $ 8.99 /month\n  * Select 1 audiobook a month from our entire collection\n  * Download your selected audiobooks for offline listening\n  * Listen to your selected audiobooks until you cancel\n  * Unused monthly selections don't roll over to the next month \nAnnual Membership  | Membership Benefits\nAudible Premium Annual – 12 Credits  | \n\n  * $149.50/year\n  * 12 credits at time of purchase to be used to redeem any title from our Premium selections\n  * Access to unlimited streaming and listening from the Audible Plus Catalog\n  * Exclusive sales and discounts on purchased titles\nAudible Premium Annual – 24 Credits  | \n\n  * $229.50/year\n  * 24 credits at time of purchase to be used to redeem any title from our Premium selections\n  * Access to unlimited streaming and listening from the Audible Plus Catalog\n  * Exclusive sales and discounts on purchased titles\n\nIf your subscription is billed through the Google Play or App Store, the price may differ from what's shown here. Payments are handled directly by Google or Apple. You can manage your Audible subscription in their respective App Stores.\n\nVisit the Audible’s membership benefits page to view all Audible membership plans, prices, and benefits details.\n\n## Can I listen to Audible titles with the Amazon Prime subscription?\n\nAudible is not included with an Amazon Prime subscription. You will need to purchase a separate Audible membership. However, Prime members do get some Audible benefits. You can try Audible Premium free and get two free audiobooks.\n\n## Sign up issues\n\nLearn how to troubleshoot Sign up issues if you cannot sign up for a free trial or for a regular Audible membership.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nLearn about the Audible Premium Membership (https://help.audible.com/s/article/learn-about-premium-plus?language=pt_BR)\nciteturn767search2 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2 months ago; Crawled: last month; You can also download your titles to listen offline. ... Visit our help center article to learn more about Audible credits. ... Note: If you sign up with a 30-day free trial, your membership will automatically renew and you’ll be charged the regular monthly price after 30 days.\n\n## Learn about the Audible Premium Membership\n\n  * Aug 20, 2026\n\nLearn about the Audible Premium Membership\n\nURL Name\n\nlearn-about-premium-plus\n\nAnswer\n\n \n\nThe name of our Premium Plus plan is changing to Premium. You may see both names used while our site is updated. Don’t worry, nothing else has changed and your member benefits remain the same.\n\n \n\nAudible is a spoken word audio entertainment company owned by Amazon. You can find many types of titles with different voices. You can easily search, save, and buy audiobooks you like. You can listen to your audiobooks through the Audible app, online player, or any compatible MP3 player.\n\nIf you like to listen to bestsellers and new releases, you might like this plan. With a regular Premium Plus monthly membership, you have access to:\n\n  * Credits: You'll receive monthly credits to buy any audiobook you want, even new releases. Running low on credits? You can buy extra credits when you run out.\n  * Finding and playing titles: It's easy to browse through audiobooks, podcasts, and Originals in the Audible library. You can stream all you want from the Plus Catalog. Want to buy individual titles? You can do that too, whether you're a member or not.\n  * Ways to listen: You can enjoy Audible content through the mobile app or online player. You can also download your titles to listen offline.\n  * Cancellation and pausing: You can cancel your plan anytime, and you can pause your Premium membership if needed. Remember that if you cancel, you'll lose access to Plus Catalog titles and any unused credits.\n  * Members-only sales and deals: you will get access to exclusive sales and deals.\n\nNote: Premium monthly membership has two options: 1 credit a month or 2 credits a month. Premium annual memberships are also available in 12 or 24 credit plans. With annual membership, you get access to all of your credits right away. Any title you get with a credit is yours to keep. Visit our Audible membership benefits page to view prices and benefit details. Visit our help center article to learn more about Audible credits.\n\nIn this article:\n\n  * How do I sign up for Premium membership?\n  * How do I sign up for Premium trial?\n  * What is the Premium plan member discount benefit?\n  * What membership plans does Audible offer?\n  * Can I listen to Audible titles with the Amazon Prime subscription?\n  * Sign up issues\n\n## How do I sign up for Premium membership?\n\nYou can sign up for Premium membership from the Audible site or through the app.\n\n### On desktop\n\n  1. Go to the Audible site.\n  2. Select Browse.\n  3. Select Plans & pricing.\n  4. Select the Audible Premium plan. You may be asked to sign in with your Amazon account.\n  5. Confirm your subscription.\n\nNote: If you sign up with a 30-day free trial, your membership will automatically renew and you’ll be charged the regular monthly price after 30 days. You can cancel anytime from your Account details page.  \n\n### In the app \n\n  1. Go to your Profile.\n  2. Select the Settings gear icon.\n  3. In the Membership section, select Details.\n  4. Select Start now. \nNote: You will be taken out of the app momentarily and redirected to Audible.com to complete the enrollment. \n  5. Select Start now. \n\nNote: You can cancel anytime. If your membership is billed through Google Play or the Apple you will need to c ancel from your  App Store or Google Play Store settings at least 24 hours in advance.   \n\n## How do I sign up for Premium trial?\n\nNew customers can sign up for a Premium free trial from the Audible site or through the app for iOS users. After 30 days, your membership will automatically renew and you’ll be charged the regular monthly price. You can cancel anytime from your Account details page.\n\n### On desktop\n\n  1. Go to the Audible site.\n  2. Select the Premiumplan.\n  3. Select Start my free trial.\n  4. Sign in with your Amazon account.\n  5. Select your payment method.\n  6. Select Try for $0.00.   \n\n### In the app:\n\n  1. Open the Audible app.\n  2. Sign in with your Amazon account.\n  3. Select Join. \n  4. Select Try for $0.00.\nNote: You will be taken out of the app momentarily and redirected to Audible.com to complete the enrollment. \n  5. Select Start now.\n\nNote: You can cancel anytime from your Account details page. If your membership is billed through Google Play or the Apple you will need to c ancel from your App Store or Google Play. Remember, if you cancel your Audible membership you’ll lose access to member benefits like exclusive discounts, included titles in the Plus Catalog, and credits.\n\n## What is the Premium plan member discount benefit?\n\nAs a Premium member, you get an exclusive discount every time you buy an audiobook beyond your monthly credit. With this member discount benefit, you‘ll always pay less than the non-member price on every title in our catalog.\n\n### What are the different ways I can purchase audiobooks?\n\nAs a Premium member, you have several options:\n\n  * Use your monthly or annual credits - can be used on any audiobook, regardless of price. Credits are deposited into your account at the start of each billing cycle.\n  * Pay the member-discounted price — if you've already used your credit for the month, you can purchase any audiobook at your exclusive member price.\n  * Buy extra credits — if you're eligible, you can purchase a single credit or a bundle of credits for extra savings.\n\nYou'll see all available options on title detail pages and at checkout.\n\n### How does the member discount work?\n\nYour member discount is applied automatically to every audiobook in our collection. The discount varies by title, so you'll save more on some audiobooks and less on others—but you'll always pay less than the non-member price.\n\n## What membership plans does Audible offer?\n\nAudible offers monthly and annual membership plans.\n \n\nMonthly Membership  | Membership Benefits\nAudible Plus  | \n\n  * $7.95/month\n  * Access to unlimited streaming and listening from the Audible Plus Catalog\n  * Available only for current Audible Plus members\nAudible Premium – 1 Credit  | \n\n  * $14.95/month\n  * 1 credit per month to be used to redeem any title from our Premium selections\n  * Access to unlimited streaming and listening from the Audible Plus Catalog\n  * Exclusive sales and discounts on purchased titles\nAudible Premium – 2 Credits  | \n\n  * $22.95/month\n  * 2 credits per month to be used to redeem any title from our Premium selections\n  * Access to unlimited streaming and listening from the Audible Plus Catalog\n  * Exclusive sales and discounts on purchased titles\nAudible Standard  | \n\n  * $ 8.99 /month\n  * Select 1 audiobook a month from our entire collection\n  * Download your selected audiobooks for offline listening\n  * Listen to your selected audiobooks until you cancel\n  * Unused monthly selections don't roll over to the next month \nAnnual Membership  | Membership Benefits\nAudible Premium Annual – 12 Credits  | \n\n  * $149.50/year\n  * 12 credits at time of purchase to be used to redeem any title from our Premium selections\n  * Access to unlimited streaming and listening from the Audible Plus Catalog\n  * Exclusive sales and discounts on purchased titles\nAudible Premium Annual – 24 Credits  | \n\n  * $229.50/year\n  * 24 credits at time of purchase to be used to redeem any title from our Premium selections\n  * Access to unlimited streaming and listening from the Audible Plus Catalog\n  * Exclusive sales and discounts on purchased titles\n\nIf your subscription is billed through the Google Play or App Store, the price may differ from what's shown here. Payments are handled directly by Google or Apple. You can manage your Audible subscription in their respective App Stores.\n\nVisit the Audible’s membership benefits page to view all Audible membership plans, prices, and benefits details.\n\n## Can I listen to Audible titles with the Amazon Prime subscription?\n\nAudible is not included with an Amazon Prime subscription. You will need to purchase a separate Audible membership. However, Prime members do get some Audible benefits. You can try Audible Premium free and get two free audiobooks.\n\n## Sign up issues\n\nLearn how to troubleshoot Sign up issues if you cannot sign up for a free trial or for a regular Audible membership.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nListen on a browser (https://help.audible.com/s/article/listen-on-a-browser?language=en_US)\nciteturn767view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://help.audible.com/s/article/listen-on-a-browser?language=en_US\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 152\nL0: Loading\nL1: \nL2: Sorry to interrupt\nL3: \nL4: This page has an error. You might just need to refresh it. [Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'bind')]\nL5: \nL6: 【0†Refresh】\nL7: \nL8: Skip to Main Content\nL9: \nL10: Related topics\nL11: \nL12: Ask A Question Cloud Player Listening Ways to listen Windows\nL13: ## Listen on a browser\nL14: \nL15:   * Aug 27, 2026\nL16:   * Knowledge\nL17: \nL18: Title\nL19: \nL20: Listen on a browser\nL21: \nL22: URL Name\nL23: \nL24: listen-on-a-browser\nL25: \nL26: Answer\nL27: \nL28: You can listen to Audible on your laptop or computer with the Audible Cloud Player. Since there's no 【1†Audible app for PC】, the Cloud Player makes it easy to enjoy your titles on Windows, Mac, or any other computer.\nL29: \nL30: Why you'll love the Cloud Player:\nL31:   * Pick up right where you left off 【2†across all your devices】.\nL32:   * Start listening right away — no downloads needed.\nL33:   * No extra software to install.\nL34: \nL35: What you need is the latest version of one of these browsers:\nL36: \nL37:   * Google Chrome\nL38:   * Mozilla Firefox\nL39:   * Apple Safari\nL40:   * Microsoft Edge\nL41: \nL42: Note: The Audible Cloud Player lets you stream and listen to your titles as long as you're connected to the internet. To listen offline, visit 【3†Download titles】.\nL43: \nL44: In this article:\nL45:   * 【4†How do I listen to a title on my desktop browser?】\nL46:   * 【5†How do I listen on my mobile browser?】\nL47:   * 【6†How to fix the Cloud Player when it won’t load?】\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nListen in the car (https://help.audible.com/s/article/listen-in-the-car?language=en_US)\nciteturn767view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://help.audible.com/s/article/listen-in-the-car?language=en_US\",\"lineno\":120}); Total lines: 262\nL107: ## How do I listen in Car Mode?\nL108: \nL109: Car Mode is a feature in the Audible app for both iOS and Android. It provides a simplified listening experience including hands-free voice controls. There are only four buttons on the screen:\nL110: \nL111:   * Alexa tap to talk\nL112:   * Play/Pause\nL113:   * Go Back 30 Seconds\nL114:   * Add a Bookmark\nL115: \nL116: Note: For hands-free listening on the go, you can also use your voice with Alexa or Siri to control Audible. Turn on voice controls and try saying \"Go back 3 minutes.\"\nL117: \nL118: Turn on Car Mode\nL119:   1. Open your player in the app.\nL120:   2. Select the Car Mode icon.\nL121: \nL122: Turn off Car Mode\nL123: \nL124:   1. Select the X to exit Car Mode.\nL125: \nL126: Turn on Automatic Car Mode\nL127: \nL128: Automatic Car Mode is available in the Audible app for iOS and Android. When it's on, Car Mode will launch in your player whenever your phone connects to your car via Bluetooth.\nL129: \nL130: Note: You can also turn this feature off anytime from the same Player settings.\nL131:   1. Go to your Profile.\nL132:   2. Select the Settings gear icon.\nL133:   3. Select Player.\nL134:   4. Turn on Automatic Car Mode.\nL135: ## How do I listen with Waze?\nL136: \nL137: The Audible app for both iOS and Android is compatible with any Waze version 4.69 or higher.\nL138: \nL139: Allow Waze integration in the Audible app\nL140: \nL141:   1. Go to your Profile.\nL142:   2. Select the Settings gear icon.\nL143:   3. Select Connect to other apps.\nL144:   4. Toggle on Waze integration.\nL145: \nL146: Allow Audible integration in the Waze app\nL147: \nL148:   1. Open Waze.\nL149:   2. Go to Settings.\nL150:   3. Select Audio player.\nL151:   4. Toggle on Show on the map.\nL152: \nL153: How to play titles in the Waze app\nL154: You can skip forward and back, play, and pause your Audible titles within the Waze app.\nL155: \nL156:   1. Open Waze.\nL157:   2. Select the Audio player icon.\nL158:   3. Select Audible and allow it to connect to Audible.\nL159:   4. Select Show list to view your 8 most recent titles.\nL160:   5. To listen to other titles, select Open Audible.\nL161: \nL162: Note: If you need additional support using the Waze app, please visit the 【9†Waze Help Center†support.google.com】.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nLearn about Audible Plus (https://help.audible.com/s/article/learn-about-audible-plus?language=en_US)\nciteturn767view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://help.audible.com/s/article/learn-about-audible-plus?language=en_US\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 142\nL0: Loading\nL1: \nL2: Sorry to interrupt\nL3: \nL4: Uncaught TypeError: Cannot read properties of null (reading 'style')\nL5: \nL6: 【0†Refresh】\nL7: \nL8: Skip to Main Content\nL9: \nL10: Related topics\nL11: \nL12: Audible Plus Membership Plans Plans & benefits\nL13: ## Learn about Audible Plus\nL14: \nL15:   * Sep 3, 2026\nL16:   * Knowledge\nL17: \nL18: Title\nL19: \nL20: Learn about Audible Plus\nL21: \nL22: URL Name\nL23: \nL24: learn-about-audible-plus\nL25: \nL26: Answer\nL27: \nL28: Our Audible Plus membership lets you stream or download thousands of titles from the included catalog. It includes access to podcasts, audiobooks, and Audible Originals. If you enjoy podcasts and short-form content, you might enjoy this plan.\nL29: \nL30: With an Audible Plus monthly membership, you will have access to:\nL31:   * Finding and playing titles: It's easy to browse through audiobooks, podcasts, and Originals in the Audible library. You can stream all you want from the included catalog. Want to buy individual titles? You can do that too, whether you're a member or not.\nL32:   * Ways to listen: You can enjoy Audible content through the mobile app or online player. On the app, you can download your favorite titles to listen offline.\nL33:   * Cancellation and pausing: You can cancel your plan anytime. Remember that if you cancel, you'll lose access to the included catalog and any unused credits.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nUpdate your country/marketplace (https://help.audible.com/s/article/update-your-country-marketplace?language=en_US)\nciteturn767view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://help.audible.com/s/article/update-your-country-marketplace?language=en_US\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 180\nL0: Loading\nL1: \nL2: Sorry to interrupt\nL3: \nL4: Uncaught TypeError: Cannot read properties of null (reading 'style')\nL5: \nL6: 【0†Refresh】\nL7: \nL8: Skip to Main Content\nL9: \nL10: Related topics\nL11: \nL12: Account Account & billing Account details Ask A Question+1\nL13: ## Update your country/marketplace\nL14: \nL15:   * Sep 3, 2026\nL16:   * Knowledge\nL17: \nL18: Title\nL19: \nL20: Update your country/marketplace\nL21: \nL22: URL Name\nL23: \nL24: update-your-country-marketplace\nL25: \nL26: Answer\nL27: \nL28: Your Audible marketplace is determined by the country you live in. Making sure you're signed in to the right marketplace ensures you're getting tailored support for troubleshooting and account-specific inquiries. It also ensures you see region-specific titles that may be exclusive to your area as well as pricing in the right currency for your region.\nL29: Note: Coupon balances cannot be transferred across marketplaces.\nL30: \nL31: Important:\nL32:   * Changing your marketplace in the app (signing out and signing in to a different marketplace) is not the same as migrating your account. Changing your marketplace simply signs you in to a different storefront. Migrating your account permanently transfers your membership, credits, and purchased titles to a new marketplace.\n"
